      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "**Zenith Smart Hub Troubleshooting Guide: Error 404: Connectivity Lost**\n\n1.  **Initial System Assessment:** Verify that the Zenith Smart Hub is powered on and that all indicator lights are illuminated, noting any unusual flashing patterns.\n2.  **Power Cycle Procedure Initiation:** Locate the main power adapter connected to the Zenith Smart Hub unit.\n3.  **Complete Power Disconnection:** Unplug the power adapter completely from the wall outlet or the hub itself, ensuring a full physical disconnection.\n4.  **Wait Period Adherence:** Allow a minimum of sixty (60) seconds to permit the internal capacitors to fully discharge and the system memory to clear completely.\n5.  **Reconnection Sequence Commencement:** Reinsert the power adapter securely into the wall outlet, ensuring a firm and stable connection.\n6.  **System Boot Monitoring:** Observe the Zenith Smart Hub as it begins its boot-up sequence, watching for the return of stable indicator lights.\n7.  **Network Re-establishment Attempt:** Once the hub appears stable, check the associated mobile application to confirm that the \"Error 404: Connectivity Lost\" message has been successfully cleared.\n8.  **Advanced Network Check (",
